    …
      27→# Install
      28→Install the API module as a dependency in your project so you can easily use it to query Operations Orchestration REST API
      30→```javascript
      31→npm install -g dockly
      32→```
      34→# Usage
      35→
      36→Just fire up dockly and it will automatically connect to your localhost docker daemon through the unix socket:
      37→
      38→```
      39→dockly
      40→```
      41→
      42→## Command line options:
      43→
      44→It's also possible to provide command line options for dockly to customize the docker connection
      45→
      46→| Param | Type | Description |
      47→| --- | --- | --- |
      48→| -s or --socketPath | string | Docker socket to connect to |
      49→| -H or --host | string | Remote docker daemon host to connect to |
      50→| -P or --port | string | Remote docker port to connect to  |
      51→| -T or --protocol | `http` \| `https` \| `ssh` | Remote docker protocol to connect to |
      52→| --containerFilters | string | String to apply to filter shown containers |
      53→| -h or --help | null | Display help |
      54→| -v or --version | null | Display version information |
      55→
      56→### `--containerFilters`
      57→
      58→This is a string that could be used to filter the shown containers;
      59→its format is in the x-www-form-urlencoded style and the filters you could apply are listed here: [https://docs.docker.com/engine/api/v1.37/#operation/ContainerList](https://docs.docker.com/engine/api/v1.37/#operation/ContainerList)
      60→
      61→Example: `--containerFilters="name=test&status=running"` to only show *running* container which name match *test*.
      63→# Docker Support
      64→
      65→## Run from docker
      66→
      67→You can run dockly using docker:
      68→
      69→```
      70→docker run -it --rm -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock lirantal/dockly
      71→```
      72→
      73→
      74→## Build
      75→
      76→If you wish to build dockly as a docker image yourself, you can run the following:
      77→
      78→```
      79→$ docker build -t dockly .
      80→
      81→$ docker run -it --rm --name dockly -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock dockly
      82→```
